# 0. Simple Web Stack

## 1. User Request Journey & Diagram

When a user wants to access `www.foobar.com`:
1. The user types `www.foobar.com` into their web browser.
2. The browser requests a DNS server to resolve the domain name `www.foobar.com` into an IP address.
3. The DNS server responds with IP address `8.8.8.8`.
4. The browser initiates an HTTP/HTTPS connection to server `8.8.8.8` via TCP/IP.
5. Nginx receives the HTTP request and routes dynamic requests to the Application Server.
6. The Application Server executes the codebase, queries MySQL if needed, and generates an HTTP response.
7. Nginx sends the HTTP response back to the user's browser.

